Package: stat2rmarkdown
Title: Shared Core Utilities for Statistical Software to R Markdown Converters
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Gilad", "Feldman", email = "giladfel@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2990-8997"))
Description: Common utilities for converting statistical software output files
    to reproducible R Markdown reports. Provides R Markdown document assembly,
    variable quoting, output directory management, and logging utilities shared
    across the stata2rmarkdown, spss2rmarkdown, jasp2rmarkdown, and
    jamovi2rmarkdown packages.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/giladfeldman/2rmarkdown
BugReports: https://github.com/giladfeldman/2rmarkdown/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    glue (>= 1.6.0),
    stringr (>= 1.5.0)
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    knitr
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Config/testthat/edition: 3
VignetteBuilder: knitr
